claim.claim-text:
determining (304) whether a dynamic user profile (220) is to transition from a first state to a second state based, at least in part, on one or more sensed indicators (224), wherein said second state comprises a previously unknown state, and said dynamic user profile (220) being indicative of a current inferable user behavior context for a user co-located with said mobile device (102);
transitioning (308) said dynamic user profile (220) from said first state to said second state in response to a determination that said dynamic user profile (220) is to transition from said first state to said second state; and
operatively affecting (310) one or more functions (118) performed, at least in part, by said mobile device (102) based, at least in part, on said transition of said dynamic user profile (220) from said first state to said second state;
wherein determining (304) whether said dynamic user profile (220) is to transition from said first state to said second state further comprises:
determining whether said one or more sensed indicators (224) matches one or more stored patterns or models of behavior (228) previously associated with at least said first state; and
in response to a determination that said one or more sensed indicators (224) does not match said one or more stored patterns or models of behavior (228) previously associated with at least said first state, determining that said dynamic user profile (220) is to transition from said first state to said second state;

means (116) for determining whether a dynamic user profile (220) is to transition from a first state to a second state based, at least in part, on one or more sensed indicators (224), wherein said second state comprises a previously unknown state, and said dynamic user profile (220) being indicative of a current inferable user behavior context for a user co-located with said mobile device (102);
means (116) for transitioning said dynamic user profile (220) from said first state to said second state, in response to a determination that said dynamic user profile (220) is to transition from said first state to said second state;
means (116) for operatively affecting one or more functions (118) performed, at least in part, by said mobile device (102) based, at least in part, on said transition of said dynamic user profile (220) from said first state to said second state;
means for storing one or more patterns or models of behavior (228) previously associated with at least said first state;
means for determining whether said one or more sensed indicators (224) matches said one or more stored patterns or models of behavior (228) previously associated with at least said first state;
means for determining that said dynamic user profile (220) is to transition from said first state to said second state, in response to a determination that said one or more sensed indicators (224) does not match said one or more stored patterns or models of behavior (228) previously associated with at least said first state; and
means for, in response to a determination that said one or more sensed indicators (224) does not match said one or more stored patterns or models of behavior (228) previously associated with at least said first state, establishing and learning said previously unknown state based, at least in part, on said one or more sensed indicators (224).
